 "text": "Sam was reading under his favorite tree when the pages started to glow. Then something rose out of the book. A door. Sam didn't think twice. He jumped and he landed 10 years in the future. A helicopter came down on the lawn and outstepped. Sam, 10 years older. His own company. The house. Every dream he once wrote in that book had come true. But how? The book pulled Sam back, page by page, to where it all began. One ordinary night, Sam wrote his dream down. Build my own company. It looked impossible. He wrote it anyway. The next morning, the alarm rang. He could hit snooze and sleep till 10, or get up and give his dream one hour. So which one? He got up. That night, his phone was calling. Three hours of scrolling, or one hour of building. He picked building. And then he picked it again. And again. Every single day. But not every choice was right. His first company failed. It hurt. But it wasn't the end. It was a lesson. So he adjusted and chose again. Day 1204. His first big client. Every scene was a choice. Some split his path apart. Some brought it back together. And all of them led to the same place. Then Sam was back under the tree. Same book. The first page was blank. So he wrote it down. Sam's story started on one page. Yours can too. Write your dreams and visions in one place. Break them into small steps and document your journey. Start yours. Undeam your.",
